2024-03-27T19:59:07 |From b451fd39a6f49cc9442c5c6ef000d00e7fe715d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
2024-03-27T19:59:07 |From: Richard Leach <richardleach@users.noreply.github.com>
2024-03-27T19:59:07 |Date: Tue, 18 Jul 2023 21:43:19 +0000
2024-03-27T19:59:07 |Subject: [PATCH] Perl_av_extend_guts: Zero() trailing elements after unshift &
2024-03-27T19:59:07 | resize
2024-03-27T19:59:07 |
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |Since https://github.com/Perl/perl5/commit/399fef93c903aedee05a74de780b57eeeb571b32,
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |trailing elements in an array that has been unshifted and resized
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |might not be properly Zero() initialized. This is because of faulty
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |arithmetic when calculating `to_null`, the number of elements to
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |initialize, when the array was only partially shifted.
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |This commit corrects the arithmetic, adds comments arount the
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |calculation of `to_null`, and adds a test based upon the case
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |provided in GH #21235.
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |The test added segfaults more reliably for me - almost every time -
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |than the originally supplied case. However, since it relies upon
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |uninitialized memory, it's probably still not deterministic and
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |somewhat dependent upon the choice of memory allocator.
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |Closes #21235
2024-03-27T19:59:08 |---
